      "message": "The size calculation in `get_ubo_aligned_offset` only ever impacted its own state which depended on `fCurUBOOffset`. The effective `uniformSize` value is always obtained by calling `fWriteUniform` in the following lines. This felt redundant and confusing to me as I tried to understand the code.\n\nThe logic in `fWriteUniform` is not as simple as `sksltype_to_size` but it handles array layout correctly. `UniformManager::write` calls `fWriteUniform` twice (once to compute the size and once to do actual write). The first one skips the memcpy parts since it doesn\u0027t involve a write.\n\nIt made sense to have just one way to calculate the size instead of two. Let me know if `sksltype_to_size` served a purpose that I may have missed.",
